/Author (Michael\040Axtmann\054\040Sascha\040Witt\054\040Daniel\040Ferizovic\054\040Peter\040Sanders)
/Subject (We\040present\040a\040sorting\040algorithm\040that\040works\040in\055place\054\040executes\040in\040parallel\054\040is\040cache\055efficient\054\040avoids\040branch\055mispredictions\054\040and\040performs\040work\040O\050n\040log\040n\051\040for\040arbitrary\040inputs\040with\040high\040probability\056\040The\040main\040algorithmic\040contributions\040are\040new\040ways\040to\040make\040distribution\055based\040algorithms\040in\055place\072\040On\040the\040practical\040side\054\040by\040using\040coarse\055grained\040block\055based\040permutations\054\040and\040on\040the\040theoretical\040side\054\040we\040show\040how\040to\040eliminate\040the\040recursion\040stack\056\040Extensive\040experiments\040shw\040that\040our\040algorithm\040IPSSSSo\040scales\040well\040on\040a\040variety\040of\040multi\055core\040machines\056\040We\040outperform\040our\040closest\040in\055place\040competitor\040by\040a\040factor\040of\040up\040to\0403\056\040Even\040as\040a\040sequential\040algorithm\054\040we\040are\040up\040to\0401\0565\040times\040faster\040than\040the\040closest\040sequential\040competitor\054\040BlockQuicksort\056)
